WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.700
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.700 --> 00:08.270
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.270 --> 00:16.180
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.350 --> 00:27.990
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.990 --> 00:33.900
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.900 --> 00:42.840
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.840 --> 00:47.540
Like the wind

00:47.540 --> 00:50.650
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.650 --> 00:54.150
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.150 --> 01:00.690
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.690 --> 01:07.430
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.430 --> 01:13.570
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.570 --> 01:20.240
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.240 --> 01:27.550
The roadless journey continues

01:56.780 --> 01:59.150
There was once a physicist
who published a new theory

01:59.150 --> 02:04.720
that shattered existing common-sense
notions of thermodynamics.

02:04.720 --> 02:07.390
Assuming an imaginary entity that
observes the movement of molecules,

02:07.390 --> 02:10.390
he concluded that it was
possible to control molecules.

02:10.390 --> 02:15.660
In other words, that entropy could be decreased.

02:15.660 --> 02:20.500
The physicist called the entity
that controlled molecules a demon,

02:20.500 --> 02:25.600
and named the theory after himself,
calling it "Maxwell's demon."

02:29.280 --> 02:31.110
However, subsequently,

02:31.110 --> 02:34.650
through close scrutiny by prominent scholars,

02:34.650 --> 02:36.580
it was concluded that Maxwell's demon was,

02:36.580 --> 02:39.020
in all practicality, impossible.

02:39.020 --> 02:41.080
And the theory was debunked.

02:56.440 --> 02:58.460
A phone call for you, ma'am.

03:16.490 --> 03:18.120
Hey!

04:13.750 --> 04:15.380
Fortune telling...

04:25.230 --> 04:28.430
- Aren't you going to eat?
- All we have is soup?

04:28.430 --> 04:30.900
Would you rather we had bread, too?

04:30.900 --> 04:32.920
That would be better.

04:42.080 --> 04:43.700
Welcome.

04:46.580 --> 04:49.250
- A beer and a milk.
- Eh?

04:49.250 --> 04:51.590
You got anything to eat?

04:51.590 --> 04:52.990
Something not spicy.

04:52.990 --> 04:55.060
How about some enchiladas?

04:55.060 --> 04:57.930
That'll be fine. Give me two.

04:57.930 --> 04:59.420
You got it.

05:34.600 --> 05:39.660
Looks like we better take
our time eating, Lirio.

06:05.390 --> 06:07.330
Your money here.

06:14.970 --> 06:18.740
I've never seen such an
unsociable street performer.

06:18.740 --> 06:20.800
It's fresh in a way.

06:22.310 --> 06:23.540
That's all?

06:23.540 --> 06:25.880
Huh?

06:25.880 --> 06:27.850
I can't even buy bread.

06:33.520 --> 06:35.320
- What?
- Those.

06:35.320 --> 06:37.330
You don't get these.

06:37.330 --> 06:39.020
Right.

06:40.860 --> 06:43.330
So you're not even going to thank me?

06:43.330 --> 06:46.370
Thank you? Why?

06:46.370 --> 06:48.600
Why? Because...

06:48.600 --> 06:51.840
- Sheesh...
- Oh, well.

06:51.840 --> 06:53.670
That's my line.

06:53.670 --> 06:56.180
- Oh, wait!
- Show's over for today.

06:56.180 --> 06:58.180
No, that's not it.

06:58.180 --> 07:00.620
Wait, hold on a minute there.

07:00.620 --> 07:02.350
I'm not taking any disciples.

07:02.350 --> 07:05.290
Like I'd want to be one!

07:05.290 --> 07:07.520
You're Ellis, aren't you?

07:07.520 --> 07:08.850
What?

07:10.020 --> 07:12.190
I finally found you.

07:12.190 --> 07:15.600
You're wrong. I'm not Ellis.

07:15.600 --> 07:17.790
It's no use playing dumb.

07:21.800 --> 07:24.910
She's a pretty girl. Who is she?

07:24.910 --> 07:27.710
It's you, no matter how you look at it.

07:27.710 --> 07:30.040
But I'm not Ellis.

07:30.040 --> 07:33.110
Whatever. Just come with me quietly.

07:33.110 --> 07:35.220
There's a bounty on your head.

07:35.220 --> 07:39.240
- Bounty?
- Come on, before the others get here.

07:50.100 --> 07:52.900
Hand that girl over to me.

07:52.900 --> 07:54.940
Too late, I guess.

07:54.940 --> 07:56.430
Hand her over.

08:07.680 --> 08:09.420
Wh-Why, you!

08:09.420 --> 08:10.990
I won't insist on taking your lives.

08:10.990 --> 08:13.650
Get lost. You're dismissed.

08:24.000 --> 08:25.970
What did you do that for?

08:25.970 --> 08:28.960
Small fry don't deserve to live.

08:30.610 --> 08:32.630
Ellis, watch out!

08:37.710 --> 08:39.370
Be a good girl now.

08:42.280 --> 08:43.770
Ellis!

08:45.790 --> 08:47.650
Hey, you okay?!

08:49.460 --> 08:51.150
That damn woman!

08:52.860 --> 08:55.160
Ellis.

08:55.160 --> 08:57.630
- Why?
- Huh?

08:57.630 --> 09:00.570
They came shooting at me.

09:00.570 --> 09:04.340
Those guys mean to save themselves the trouble.

09:04.340 --> 09:06.340
Dead or alive.

09:06.340 --> 09:09.480
In other words, it doesn't
matter if you're dead.

09:09.480 --> 09:12.670
They could hand over your
body and still get the bounty.

09:14.220 --> 09:17.320
A terrible way to treat a girl, isn't it?

09:17.320 --> 09:19.420
Even dead...

09:19.420 --> 09:21.080
Ellis?

09:27.030 --> 09:29.390
No way... For real?

09:38.370 --> 09:39.930
Rosenberg.

09:41.780 --> 09:43.840
So you found her.

09:43.840 --> 09:45.740
I'm glad to hear that.

09:47.180 --> 09:50.020
They're trying to kill her?

09:50.020 --> 09:53.920
It can't be helped.
That was the deal, after all.

09:55.190 --> 09:56.520
Yes.

09:56.520 --> 09:59.020
Then, please contact me again.

10:07.470 --> 10:09.200
Kill her...

10:11.940 --> 10:14.130
What do you think of that?

10:17.210 --> 10:18.480
Rosenberg.

10:18.480 --> 10:22.720
Um, I'm Hayward of the Audit Department.

10:22.720 --> 10:26.090
- I contacted you the other
day about this matter, but...
- Ah, Miss Hayward.

10:26.090 --> 10:29.790
I apologize, but I will call you back later.

10:29.790 --> 10:33.390
I must go to a party hosted by the governor now.

10:33.390 --> 10:35.760
What? Uh, um...

10:35.760 --> 10:38.400
I am busy.

10:38.400 --> 10:40.940
What'd he say? Is he coming over?

10:40.940 --> 10:42.940
He said he would call back later.

10:42.940 --> 10:45.610
Later? You've got to be kidding me.

10:45.610 --> 10:49.340
You listen to me. Make sure he
comes to see me within the hour.

10:49.340 --> 10:50.580
Make sure of it.

10:50.580 --> 10:54.420
Like hell we can permit any more of these
ambiguous investigative expenses!

10:54.420 --> 10:55.810
Sheesh!

10:56.820 --> 10:59.750
- Um, what are these?
- Huh?

10:59.750 --> 11:02.760
Oh, take care of those account
statements, too, would you?

11:02.760 --> 11:04.690
There are a couple things that don't add up.

11:04.690 --> 11:07.460
- Follow up on them.
- What? But...

11:07.460 --> 11:11.090
That damn Rosenberg ticks me off!

11:38.290 --> 11:40.280
So she's made contact.

12:02.220 --> 12:05.520
I've never done corn fortune
telling before. Is it accurate?

12:05.520 --> 12:08.220
In the old days, they used to call me a witch.

12:08.220 --> 12:11.260
- A witch?
- Hold out your hands.

12:11.260 --> 12:13.320
Oh, okay.

12:15.900 --> 12:20.030
Spread them out, like you're drawing a line.

12:20.030 --> 12:21.560
Okay.

12:30.010 --> 12:32.170
Will I be rich?

12:34.680 --> 12:36.220
No?

12:36.220 --> 12:38.090
I'd like to be...

12:38.090 --> 12:41.020
And I thought Ellis was strange...

12:41.020 --> 12:45.690
Your fortune is most unusual, too.

12:45.690 --> 12:46.760
Huh?

12:46.760 --> 12:49.360
You're going to lead a life
full of ups and downs.

12:49.360 --> 12:51.530
My life's already like that.

12:51.530 --> 12:53.230
I meant your future.

12:53.230 --> 12:56.140
Even more varied things
will happen in your future.

12:56.140 --> 13:01.380
What?! I don't want that!
I want to find happiness!

13:01.380 --> 13:05.050
It's not as if everything that
will happen will mean misfortune.

13:05.050 --> 13:07.580
The key will be in how you handle it.

13:07.580 --> 13:09.720
Make it all happy for me.

13:09.720 --> 13:11.320
You're a witch, aren't you, granny?

13:11.320 --> 13:13.620
Do something about it with your magic.

13:13.620 --> 13:17.760
Poof, you know? Poof, and just do it.

13:17.760 --> 13:20.460
I wasn't trying to make you laugh.

13:20.460 --> 13:25.730
You just may be the one I can entrust Ellis to.

13:25.730 --> 13:27.400
Huh?

13:27.400 --> 13:29.900
She's a good girl.

13:29.900 --> 13:34.070
She was born under a slightly odd star, but...

13:36.610 --> 13:38.480
She's a good girl.

13:54.090 --> 13:55.580
Sorry!

13:58.630 --> 14:00.870
It seems she wants to go south.

14:00.870 --> 14:03.640
South? South where?

14:03.640 --> 14:05.110
No idea.

14:05.110 --> 14:09.340
She doesn't even seem to really know herself.

14:09.340 --> 14:12.280
She had a destination, and yet...

14:12.280 --> 14:15.870
I guess she just couldn't
ignore a feeble old woman.

14:28.530 --> 14:31.170
- Are you going?
- Yes.

14:31.170 --> 14:33.800
She's not coming back, is she?

14:33.800 --> 14:35.640
She's being pursued, so...

14:35.640 --> 14:37.700
Protect her for me.

14:39.640 --> 14:41.980
I'm counting on you.

14:41.980 --> 14:43.470
Right...

15:05.170 --> 15:06.660
Let's go.

15:08.870 --> 15:10.070
Oh!

15:10.070 --> 15:12.010
Be gentler with me!

15:12.010 --> 15:13.070
What is this?!

15:13.070 --> 15:16.110
We haven't done anything
to deserve being investigated!

15:16.110 --> 15:19.410
- Shut up! Hands forward! Spread your legs!
- What? Wait! Oh, wait! Honestly!

15:19.410 --> 15:21.850
- Woohoo, looking good there!
- I said, shut up!

15:21.850 --> 15:23.850
Now, just get arrested!

15:23.850 --> 15:26.520
You guys are just too suspicious!

15:26.520 --> 15:27.920
Oh, this?

15:27.920 --> 15:29.420
It's just a scratch.

15:29.420 --> 15:31.590
It's closed up already.

15:31.590 --> 15:34.030
- Take that.
- Owowowowow!

15:35.030 --> 15:36.900
Liar.

15:36.900 --> 15:39.560
It opened up because you poked it!

15:44.440 --> 15:46.070
Thanks.

15:47.370 --> 15:50.710
Is Granny... okay?

15:50.710 --> 15:53.280
She will be, as long as you don't show up.

15:53.280 --> 15:56.620
She won't be killed if I don't go back...

15:56.620 --> 15:57.790
Basically.

15:57.790 --> 16:00.480
Then, I'm not going back.

16:02.560 --> 16:07.120
Well, I'll go grab your things for you later.

16:12.730 --> 16:15.760
So everyone's after me...

16:17.770 --> 16:19.800
Because I'm a murderer.

16:40.260 --> 16:42.160
What happened?

16:44.130 --> 16:46.770
It's fine if you don't want to talk about it.

16:46.770 --> 16:49.470
- I don't know.
- Huh?

16:49.470 --> 16:53.110
I don't... remember anything.

16:53.110 --> 16:54.540
I see.

16:54.540 --> 16:57.480
Oh, that reminds me...

16:57.480 --> 17:00.810
I'm Nadie. I'd forgotten to introduce myself.

17:00.810 --> 17:02.440
Nice to meet you.

17:03.720 --> 17:05.780
"Nice to meet you" is weird, huh?

17:10.290 --> 17:13.890
- It can't be...
- Granny...

17:13.890 --> 17:15.200
Ellis!

17:15.200 --> 17:17.360
It's a trap! Come back!

17:19.900 --> 17:21.890
Whoa, I can't do this...

17:31.580 --> 17:33.880
Welcome home, missy.

17:33.880 --> 17:37.550
That made a nice sound, didn't it? Boom!

17:37.550 --> 17:39.220
Move aside.

17:39.220 --> 17:43.320
I think it'd be better if you didn't look.

17:43.320 --> 17:46.030
You're coming with us.

17:46.030 --> 17:49.520
Do as we say, if you don't want to die.

17:55.400 --> 17:59.040
Put down your gun, if you don't want to die.

17:59.040 --> 18:00.440
Why, you...

18:00.440 --> 18:02.240
I'll shoot for real.

18:08.080 --> 18:11.050
If you have any last words, say them now.

18:11.050 --> 18:13.120
That's my line!

18:13.120 --> 18:14.950
Ellis, run.

18:16.390 --> 18:18.690
What are you doing? Hurry up.

18:18.690 --> 18:20.350
Ellis!

18:28.540 --> 18:30.260
Hot! That's hot!

18:38.380 --> 18:39.580
My eyes! My eyes!

18:39.580 --> 18:42.140
Ellis, what in the world did you...

18:43.620 --> 18:45.120
That hurts!

18:45.120 --> 18:48.290
- Someone call a doctor.
- Damn it all! Damn it all!

18:48.290 --> 18:50.280
My eyes!

18:56.800 --> 18:58.630
Granny...

19:01.440 --> 19:03.270
Is that you, Ellis?

19:03.270 --> 19:05.740
Yes. Ellis.

19:05.740 --> 19:07.400
Granny...

19:09.940 --> 19:13.750
Ah, I got to see you again...

19:13.750 --> 19:16.820
I must thank the gods...

19:16.820 --> 19:19.250
This is because of me.

19:19.250 --> 19:21.620
You're wrong, Ellis.

19:21.620 --> 19:24.120
None of this is your fault.

19:24.120 --> 19:26.630
It could never be your fault.

19:26.630 --> 19:28.160
Granny...

19:28.160 --> 19:30.490
It could never be your fault...

19:34.600 --> 19:37.500
This stone will guide you.

19:37.500 --> 19:39.140
What?

19:39.140 --> 19:42.170
You're going south, aren't you?

19:44.210 --> 19:46.370
Wiñay Marka.

19:50.380 --> 19:53.550
It means "place of eternity."

19:53.550 --> 19:55.350
Eternity?

20:11.470 --> 20:13.460
Splendid.

20:15.410 --> 20:17.910
To Project Leviathan.

20:17.910 --> 20:19.740
Cheers.

20:32.230 --> 20:34.350
Ellis, let's go.

20:36.330 --> 20:39.000
The bounty hunters are coming.

20:39.000 --> 20:40.930
You're one, too, aren't you?

20:40.930 --> 20:42.420
What?

20:43.670 --> 20:45.670
Oh, Ellis...

20:45.670 --> 20:47.710
Don't follow me.

20:47.710 --> 20:50.700
You'll die if you stay around me.

20:53.050 --> 20:54.540
Ellis...

20:58.020 --> 21:01.690
You can tell me not to follow you,
but I can't just say, "Okay."

21:01.690 --> 21:03.860
You want money that badly?

21:03.860 --> 21:05.860
I want money, too, but...

21:05.860 --> 21:08.360
Granny asked me to do her a favor.

21:08.360 --> 21:09.600
What?

21:09.600 --> 21:12.460
To look after this girl,
who knows nothing of the world.

21:17.870 --> 21:19.370
She should be in here!

21:19.370 --> 21:22.270
Damn little girl! Where are you?!

21:23.880 --> 21:26.250
All right, let's just get going on our journey.

21:26.250 --> 21:27.580
What?

21:27.580 --> 21:29.950
You're going south, aren't you?

21:29.950 --> 21:31.780
I'll keep you company.

21:34.390 --> 21:35.660
In exchange,

21:35.660 --> 21:38.490
once you've accomplished
your goal, you're coming with me.

21:38.490 --> 21:39.760
Okay?

21:39.760 --> 21:41.730
Oh, hey!

21:41.730 --> 21:43.800
Our jeep!

21:43.800 --> 21:46.070
Hold it right there!

21:46.070 --> 21:47.560
Hey!

22:10.190 --> 22:13.330
Wiñay Marka.

22:13.330 --> 22:16.660
Wiñay... Marka...

22:30.140 --> 22:32.280
And that is how...

22:32.280 --> 22:34.110
...the two met.

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Like flowers that never die

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
A night of red stars

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
The vanishing warmth

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
I want to keep it here

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
You, with your eyes closed

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Yearning over and over

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
...everything
